\section{Conclusion}
\label{sec:conclusion}
Conclusions to be discussed once results are analysed.

\section{Future work}
\label{sec:futurework}
For future commercial deployment, ReFit would need to support multiple concurrent users. Optimisation for systems without a GPU would be desirable, so that most machines produced within the last decade are able to run the application. Streaming the application from a desktop machine may represent a reasonable compromise between portability and the hardware limitations of mobile devices. As local models become more capable and quantisation methods improve further, the speed and robustness of the application's outputs may improve appreciably, while the storage required may fall. Machine learning capable of modelling user behaviour in order to suggest sets and repetitions, and to extrapolate potential fitness gains, represents a desirable further extension. Migrating to a CSS framework such as Tailwind would be a natural immediate next step for a project of this scale.

